th forecast . In the tender offer supplement , Dow Jones <ei28 discloses> the different growth <ei29 forecasts> but <ei30 says> it <ei31 views> the 20 % growth rate \" as a hoped-for goal \" of Telerate 's management \" and not as a realistic basis on which to project the company 's likely future performance . \" Telerate shares <ei32 fell> 50 cents on Friday to <ei34 close> at $ 20 each in New York Stock Exchange composite trading . Dow Jones shares also <ei35 fell> 50 cents to <ei36 close> at $ 36.125 in Big Board composite trading . Dow Jones has <ei37 said> it <ei38 believes> the $ 18-a-share price is <ei39 fair> to Telerate 's minority shareholders . Late last week , representatives of Dow Jones and Telerate <ei41 began> <ei42 negotiations> about the terms of the <ei43 offer> , but those <ei44 talks> did n't result in any <ei45 changes> in the offer . Telerate provides information about financial markets through an electronic network . Dow Jones , which owns 67 % of Telerate , publishes The Wall Street Journal , Barron 's magazine , community newspapers and operates financial news services and computer data bases .", "gold": [["ei10", "causes", "ei13"], ["ei44", "causes", "ei45"], ["ei13", "causedby", "ei10"], ["ei45", "causedby", "ei44"]], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei2", "ei4", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei9", "ei10", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "ei20", "ei21", "ei22", "ei23", "ei24", "ei25", "ei26", "ei27", "ei28", "ei29", "ei30", "ei31", "ei32", "ei34", "ei35", "ei36", "ei37", "ei38", "ei39", "ei41", "ei42", "ei43", "ei44", "ei45"], "surfaces": {"ei1": "extended", "ei2": "offer", "ei4": "offer", "ei5": "rejected", "ei6": "scheduled", "ei7": "expire", "ei9": "said", "ei10": "extended", "ei11": "offer", "ei12": "allow", "ei13": "review", "ei14": "mailed", "ei16": "filed", "ei17": "launched", "ei18": "offer", "ei20": "change", "ei21": "offer", "ei22": "extend", "ei23": "criticized", "ei24": "disclosing", "ei25": "expects", "ei26